WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.980
Attack with Cannon.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.480
That's game.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.020
Kazuki, you're just too damn strong!

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.900
C'mon, one more battle!

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.400
I'm not gonna quit before I win at least one battle!

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.700
Guess I won't be going home tonight.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.490
Say what?

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.280
So you're not with your sister for once, huh.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:18.990
Huh?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.370
Come on, don't put it like that.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.000
Hey guys, mind if we play too?

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.590
We picked up WIXOSS recently too,
but it's kinda hard to understand...

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.130
Kazuki-kun, aren't you good at this?

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.590
Hey, can you teach me?

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.300
Uh, sure.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.450
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:03.960
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.710
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.710
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.970
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:22.020
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.270
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:30.360
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:35.650
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:41.410
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:46.500
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.840
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.050
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:02.810
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.150
WIXOSS Party?

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.440
It's more of a get-together of sorts.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.910
Only the guys used to come before, but a lot more girls are participating these days.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:25.450
Oh, right! Why don't you three enter together?

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.830
You should totally go in matching clothes!

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.580
That'd be <i>so</i> cute! I'll help you pick them!

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.750
Momoka!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.050
Hey, there you are!

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:42.140
Anyway, you can enter the day of,
so why not go and take a look?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.890
Y-Yeah...

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.560
Hey.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.770
I'm almost done here. Just a sec, all right?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.110
Yuzuki?

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.230
Yeah...

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.030
So, what should we do about this event?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:05.160
<i>For someone without a wish to
participate as a WIXOSS Selector is...</i>

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.080
<i>blasphemy.</i>

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.330
I'll go.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.880
There may be Selectors there, you know?

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.340
Ah, but I...

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.510
Right, your wish already came true.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.680
Yes...

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:26.850
And I'd feel bad for my opponent if I were to win.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.640
Shouldn't it be fine as long as
that opponent isn't a Selector?

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.400
Besides, you can battle guys all you want.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.730
Oh, right!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.020
As long as they're not Selectors, I can battle anyone!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.070
Yeah!

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.860
All right!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.450
I-I guess... I'll enter, too...

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.870
I wanted to test my new deck anyway...

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.290
Right, Midoriko?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.540
Midoriko?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.420
Huh? Oh, right.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.630
All right, it's settled!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.220
So, what now?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.840
Wanna pick out matching clothes now that we're going?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.600
The kind idols wear, like this!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.970
But these clothes are...

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.640
Wide-neck Pullover
Tunic

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.690
Pretty expensive, huh... Scratch that idea.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.060
Hey, look!

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:17.090
Whoa, cheap! Only 100 yen!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.900
<b>limited time only
Whoa, cheap! Only 100 yen!</b>

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.900
And there's all sorts of them!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.530
How about we use these?

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.410
Scrunchies?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.120
Yeah! Clothes might be a bit too expensive...

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.160
Hey, how's this?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.160
This one's green, so it suits you!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.660
Ah... thanks!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.290
I'm getting a red one!

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.380
Ruuko, you take a white one... nevermind, none here.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.090
Well, you can have that weird-colored one.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.840
I don't want the weird-colored one!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.720
How about this one, then?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.300
That one's just as weird! Come on, Yuzuki...

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.100
Sorry, just kidding!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.930
And then we bought matching ones, and then—

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:57.900
Hitoe, I know you're happy,
but you just stepped out of the bath.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.690
You'll get kinks in your hair.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.530
I'm fine!

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:06.740
And then Ruuko really <i>was</i> about to get a weird one,
but then she picked a light blue one—

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.410
Slow down! We'll talk about that later,

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:13.000
but I need you to put on something warm and dry your hair first so you don't catch a cold.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.330
Okay!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.000
Oh, it <i>did</i> get kinked...

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.380
The scrunchie's a bit wet, too!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.380
I should have seen that one coming...

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.800
I'm such a dolt.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.890
Hitoe.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.140
What is it?

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.310
It's best you throw me away.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.230
Throw... you away?

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.480
Your wish has already come true.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.770
You don't need to battle anymore.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:47.860
T-True, but that's no reason to throw you away, Midoriko.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.410
If you keep me,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.910
something terrible may happen.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.370
No!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.090
Ruuko and Yuzuki aren't the only ones.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.630
Midoriko, you're my dear friend, too!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.760
Hitoe...

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.600
Now stop saying weird things like that.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.760
Right, the hair dryer...

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.190
It's no use...

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.730
What's the matter?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.610
Um, well...

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.030
I figured I'd tie up my hair for a change.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.240
You're a bit too clumsy for that.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.410
Here, let me do it for you.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.870
D-Don't worry, I can do it!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.580
But Yuzuki—

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.210
I'm fine! I can do it myself!

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.710
So cold...

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:47.590
Look!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.300
There's a giraffe on top of that pillar now.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:54.760
Giraffe! It's going to battle that other giraffe!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.890
Tama, all you ever think about is battling...

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.650
<i>Do you want to...</i>

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.480
<i>do it with me?</i>

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:12.200
That Iona person... she was pretty,
but also kind of scary...

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.280
I'll beat all scary people!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.090
Looks like I'm here a bit early.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.970
I just got here... I'll be waiting...

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.300
<b>I'll be waiting.
I just got here,
It's Hitoe.
Yuzuki</b>

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.680
Sending

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:43.330
Waiting here with so many people around...

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.270
It kinda makes me feel like a normal girl.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.070
You <i>are</i> a normal girl, Hitoe.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:51.150
Heh, I guess...

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.330
The weather is so nice.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:02.000
You know, when I moved to Tokyo,

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.580
I thought there wasn't much of a sky to look at with all these buildings.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.880
But there it is. A blue sky like any other.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.090
Why haven't I noticed it before?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.260
Was I...

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.890
looking down all this time?

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.100
Hitoe...

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.020
Hitoe!

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.940
Please, throw me away! Hurry!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.160
Ruuko, hurry!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.540
I'm sorry! The restroom was chock-full,

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.540
and that kid behind me said she was about to wet herself, so—

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.250
We're making Hitoe wait!

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.080
Ah, hold on!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.460
Huh? Where did she go?

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.920
This place is full of people, too!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.350
Did you find her?

00:08:59.350 --> 00:08:59.760
No...

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.230
She's not replying to my texts either.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.980
I wonder if she got angry
because we made her wait...

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.020
Hitoe's not the type to get mad over something like that.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.860
Don't you think so too, Hanayo-san?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.320
Hanayo-san?

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.150
Oh, ah, well...

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.450
Field!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.490
What's the matter, Tama?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.160
A battlefield is open somewhere!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.410
Don't tell me...

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.580
Hitoe?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.920
This opponent... she's strong!

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.140
Are you all right, Midoriko?

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.810
I'm fine...

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.520
Forgive me, Midoriko...

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.060
I won't make you suffer any more than this.
I'll try to lose as fast as I can!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.690
No! You can't give up, Hitoe!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.690
It's okay. My wish already came true.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.320
So there's no need to draw this painful battle out.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.450
Hitoe... I'm sorry.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.080
There's something I haven't told you yet.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:06.960
Midoriko?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.590
I told you that you can become an
Eternal Girl if you win three times.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:14.920
Hitoe?!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.420
Hitoe?!

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.180
S-Sorry...

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.470
Where are you?!
S-Sorry...

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:25.390
But if you <i>lose</i> three times...

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.550
Is it around here, Tama?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.470
The battlefield is gone.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.560
Hey, Hanayo-san? Do you know anything?

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.100
Look there.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.610
Hitoe!
Hitoe!

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:18.940
Hitoe!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.650
What's the matter? We were looking all over for—

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.740
Hey, Hitoe?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.830
Wh-What is it?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.000
Why do you know my name?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.920
What are you talking about, Hitoe?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:35.750
Wait!

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.220
What's wrong, Hitoe?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.430
Hitoe, are you hurt somewhere?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.020
No! Don't touch her!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.860
Wh-Who are you?

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.030
Wait!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.990
Hitoe lost.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:05.870
Tama?

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.450
Hitoe doesn't smell like a Selector. She lost the battle.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.170
She's not a Selector anymore?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.000
What's this about?! Why is she like that?!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.510
Is it because she lost three times?!

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.880
Hanayo-san!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.680
It's not just that your wish doesn't
come true when you lose three times;

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.770
your wish is reversed.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.690
The wish... is reversed?

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:35.520
Yes.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:39.530
Let's say that you wish to acquire great wealth.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:46.910
Losing your battles means that you'll be stripped of everything and fall into poverty.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.410
If we say that your wish is to master the piano,

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:57.880
you would lose your instrument or
become incapacitated in some way.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.130
In any case, you wouldn't ever be able to play it again.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.420
That's horrible...

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.180
I... I just don't understand.
What happened to Hitoe, then?!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.350
Hitoe's wish was to make friends.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.100
And when you reverse her wish...

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.440
She loses... her friends?

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:21.280
That's not all.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.150
She will never make friends again.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.200
You saw what happened to Hitoe.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:31.490
When someone with the potential to become her friend approaches her,

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.620
her body reacts with immense pain.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.830
That can't be true!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.250
And now, with her third loss,

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.840
the battle for her wish has ended.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:47.800
All the memories she made during
her time as a Selector have disappeared.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.810
<i>I'm scared... I'm scared... I'm scared!</i>

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.850
<i>What's wrong, Hitoe? </i>

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.480
<i>Who... were those girls? </i>

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.910
<i>It didn't hurt.</i>

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.370
<i>Why?</i>

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.420
<i>It hurts, it hurts... it hurts!</i>

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:27.380
<i>I'm scared! I don't want to think anymore! I don't...!</i>

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.100
I've decided.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.600
I'll wish for Hitoe to go back to normal again!

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.860
That will be my wish!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.440
Right, that would—

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:45.610
That's illicit.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:55.830
No wish granted through Selector battles—
whether fulfilled or reversed—can be undone.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.330
Hanayo-san...

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.330
Why did you keep something that important a secret?!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:05.630
Why aren't you answering me?! Hanayo-san!

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.140
Man...

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.020
The sky is overcast with clouds now.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.110
Looks like it's going to rain.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.490
I don't have the right to cry.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:36.200
I've ripped your most precious wish from your heart.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.420
I loved you, Hitoe.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:56.310
I wish I hadn't been your LRIG, Hitoe...

00:15:58.430 --> 00:15:59.730
Farewell.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.380
You scare me, Hanayo-san...

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.510
I trusted you all this time.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.970
You can throw me away.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.930
It's fine, Yuzuki. You can throw me away.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:42.730
Shut up!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.110
Yuzuki?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:50.730
What's the matter?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.990
Uh... it's nothing...

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.070
Were you fighting with Hanayo-san?

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:01.540
Yuzuki, you've been acting strange lately.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.920
You used to tell me about everything.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.090
<i>Not </i>everything<i>.</i>

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.170
I want you to talk with me again and to rely on me again.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:13.380
<i>I can't tell you what I truly feel.</i>

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.680
We've been together all this time.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.840
<i>If I say it now...</i>

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.350
Yuzuki?

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.980
It's nothing. Really, there's nothing wrong!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.530
So you won't tell me no matter what...

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.910
It's about time I stopped hanging off my sister, too.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.160
Kazu—

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:46.370
Hello? Ah, yeah, I'm fine.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.590
Tomorrow? Everyone's going to come?

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.380
No, I'm not really busy...

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.340
All right, I'll be there.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.140
Right. See you.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:07.060
No... Please, no...

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.880
This is Tama's first time at this kind of place!

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:19.240
I've only been to family restaurants with Grandma before.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.200
You're not going home?

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.990
Grandma's really sharp...

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:28.120
She sees right through me when I hide failed tests and stuff.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.500
Ruu...

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.920
Tama, did you know?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.150
Tama doesn't know a lot.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:41.050
There's a part in my head that goes white when I try to think.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:45.220
Tama loves battles! I want to battle more! Much more!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:49.120
But I don't want to see Ruu sad.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.400
Tama...

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.130
<i>There</i> you are!

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:57.150
Piruluk told me there's been a battle around here.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:02.280
I thought Ruu-Ruu and the others could be involved, so I mailed Yuzu-pon and Hittoe,

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.990
but only Hittoe replied!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.790
Funny thing is, she doesn't remember a thing!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:08.410
<b>What do you mean by battle?
Who is this?
If this is a prank, please stop.
Subject: How was your battle?
From: Hittoe</b>

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.870
I guess she's not a Selector anymore.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.500
You knew this is what happens when you lose?!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.380
What was that?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.880
What's going on?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:17.710
Come with me.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.430
Let's tinkle together!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.640
A-Akira-san...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:27.770
The first battlefield I encountered wasn't for my own battle.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:28.730
Huh?

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:35.690
When I was on my way back from a shoot,
Iona was just about to battle another Selector,

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.860
and I got pulled into that field.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.780
The opposing Selector had already lost
two battles and was at the end of her line.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:52.460
She looked pretty sick, you know, and she was huffing and puffing trying to win the battle.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:59.090
Well, Iona still beat that tragic heroine real bad.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:08.890
After that she had this huge seizure, and there
were like, ambulances and stuff all over the place!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:14.270
Iona's LRIG is quite a sadistic character, y'know? Poor girl...

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.520
S-So, what happened to that girl...?

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.940
No idea. They took her to the hospital.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.610
But from the looks of it...

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.120
That's... terrible...

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:30.660
Like, <i>seriously</i>, right? Compared to that...

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.620
not being able to make friends ever again is just... you know?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.080
H-How did you...?!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.710
Did you forget?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:41.090
I saw her wish in our last battle.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:45.010
Well, Hittoe was a hyper-loner anyway.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:49.560
<i>You</i> should be happy, though. Now you don't have to bother with her royal slowness.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.180
They'd just have started bullying you, too.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.020
And hey, now she knows what she can and can't do.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:59.480
Like, it's totally impossible for her. She's so gross!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:04.070
Even if she doesn't ever make friends again, it's not like that's a problem.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.990
Not a problem?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.660
Right, so—

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:09.490
Take that back!

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.870
Nopey-nopey!

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:16.370
Take that back!

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.630
I'll never forgive you if you don't take that back!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.630
Huh? You won't forgive me?

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:25.550
It doesn't matter if Ruu-Ruu forgives me or not.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.640
That doesn't faze good old Aki-lucky!

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:34.890
Say, how about we battle if you really can't forgive me.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:40.270
If you give me a good beating, I just totally might feel like apologizing.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.570
Fine...

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.280
Ruu?

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:48.530
I'll battle... and I'll make you apologize to Hitoe...

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:51.450
I'll make you apologize to my friend!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.960
That
Vow
is
Illicit

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:28.510
Hitoe lost three times...

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:30.220
You're the worst!

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:31.430
What's that to you?

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.800
No... no, no!

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:35.060
Why would you care?

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:37.140
I'm not scared of anything!

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:37.160
This
Heart
is
Pure White
I'm not scared of anything!

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.930
This heart is pure white.
